      "title": "Short statements: subject and verb",
      "explanation": "An English statement needs a subject (who or what) and a finite verb (the verb with its tense and agreement). The subject normally comes before the verb: Anna works. In the present simple, add -s to the verb after he, she, it or a singular name: Anna lives in London. After I, you, we, they or a plural noun, use the base verb: We play football. The children sleep.",
